        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-9143-1",
        "name": "USN-9143-1",
        "description": "It was discovered that the Murmur server in Mumble did not rate limit certain client messages. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause Murmur to hang or crash, resulting in a denial of service. This update adds a message rate limit, which can be configured with the messageburst and messagelimit settings.",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2018-20743"
        ]
      },
